From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:00:41 +0000
Subject: MIPS: smp-cps: leave the fabric alone on intel-mips

cps_smp_setup() establishes the coherence environment for core 0: it
forces a coherent cache attribute, calls mips_cps_core_init(), joins the
core to the coherence domain and allocates the CPS exception vectors.

On intel-mips the boot chain has already done all of it before the
kernel is entered, so none of it is the kernel's to redo. The core
arrives with a coherent write-back attribute selected and already joined
to the coherence domain, which leaves the attribute force and the domain
write restating the state the platform is running on, and
mips_cps_core_init() would rewrite TCHALT, TCBIND and VPECONF0 on the
live core to get there. The CPS vectors are unused for a separate
reason: this SoC releases its secondary VPEs through a firmware mailbox,
and the CPS reset path could not reach them in any case, because a
freshly reset core decodes GCR_Cx_RESET_BASE under legacy segmentation,
which on this SoC addresses no RAM.

Skip the block when CONFIG_INTEL_MIPS is enabled. The fallback chain is
safe: core_entry_reg stays zero, and cps_prepare_cpus() checks it and
self-disables before releasing any core, so no secondary is started
against an unset vector.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-4-7
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/kernel/smp-cps.c b/arch/mips/kernel/smp-cps.c
index e2094922cec0..d28d50631caa 100644
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/smp-cps.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/smp-cps.c
@@ -266,20 +266,28 @@ static void __init cps_smp_setup(void)
 		__cpu_logical_map[v] = v;
 	}
 
-	/* Set a coherent default CCA (CWB) */
-	change_c0_config(CONF_CM_CMASK, 0x5);
+	/*
+	 * Skip the CPS fabric writes on intel-mips: the firmware boot chain
+	 * establishes CM membership and the coherent CCA before the kernel is
+	 * entered, and re-programming either from cached code is neither
+	 * necessary nor safe here.
+	 */
+	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_INTEL_MIPS)) {
+		/* Set a coherent default CCA (CWB) */
+		change_c0_config(CONF_CM_CMASK, 0x5);
 
-	/* Initialise core 0 */
-	mips_cps_core_init();
+		/* Initialise core 0 */
+		mips_cps_core_init();
 
-	/* Make core 0 coherent with everything */
-	write_gcr_cl_coherence(0xff);
+		/* Make core 0 coherent with everything */
+		write_gcr_cl_coherence(0xff);
 
-	if (allocate_cps_vecs())
-		pr_err("Failed to allocate CPS vectors\n");
+		if (allocate_cps_vecs())
+			pr_err("Failed to allocate CPS vectors\n");
 
-	if (core_entry_reg && mips_cm_revision() >= CM_REV_CM3)
-		write_gcr_bev_base(core_entry_reg);
+		if (core_entry_reg && mips_cm_revision() >= CM_REV_CM3)
+			write_gcr_bev_base(core_entry_reg);
+	}
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_MIPS_MT_FPAFF
 	/* If we have an FPU, enroll ourselves in the FPU-full mask */
